# What a deployed container runs. Nothing else.
#
# Three requirement sets exist and the boundary between them is what each one
# is FOR, not taste:
#
#   requirements.in          development and CI -- adds pytest and Streamlit
#   requirements-dev.in      the linter and the dependency auditor
#   requirements-runtime.in  this one: the API and the worker, in a container
#   api/requirements.txt     the Vercel function, which is narrower again
#                            because @vercel/python installs from the file
#                            beside the entrypoint and a serverless bundle has
#                            a size limit
#
# Streamlit is the reason this file exists rather than reusing requirements.in.
# It pulls pandas, numpy, pyarrow and altair -- hundreds of megabytes into every
# image layer, every pull and every cold start, to ship an MVP UI that the
# React SPA replaced (ADR-0015). pytest is the other: shipping the test runner
# to production is how a slow start and a wider attack surface both happen.
#
# Regenerate:
#   uv pip compile requirements-runtime.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#       -o requirements-runtime.txt
fastapi==0.141.1
uvicorn[standard]==0.52.4
sqlalchemy==2.0.52
alembic==1.19.1
psycopg2-binary==2.9.12
pydantic==2.13.4
pydantic-settings==2.15.0
pyyaml==6.0.3
